      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Development kicked off in the 1850s when the Louisville‑Lexington turnpike and the Louisville‑Frankfort railroad cut through the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crescent_Hill%2C_Louisville",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Crescent Hill’s Historic District, bounded by Brownsboro, Lexington, Peterson, Zorn, Frankfort, and Crabbs, joined the National Register in 1982.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crescent_Hill%2C_Louisville",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The stately Crescent Hill Reservoir and Park, built in 1879, remain a local mecca for residents today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
